{"kind":"propose","text":"Proposal for ordinary adoption, replacing 0b8a9ff5 (#20195) under request e855a8ca (#20301, case C of #20008); the design is notes/2026-09-07-previous-frontier-readers.md at exact 7628c518bb2fffab2597f0084f220f4dc642981c (artifact 33c335a1). Source finding: a rebuild is reported only during a full cold audit, and during a full cold audit the resident holds no same-profile snapshot whose head is the verified base of the history being audited (a restart holds nothing, a rewind holds a frontier the ref no longer has, a profile change is forbidden), so no mechanical exposure of retained state can give a first-time reader a truthful previous frontier; the earlier ancestry check would never admit anything. Decision requested, one of two: (A, recommended) decline the previous-frontier surface; a first-time reader during a full cold audit sees progress only, an already-open browser keeps its qualified status as delivered by #20008, and this note plus a reading-view paragraph are the final guidance, with no source change. (B) adopt the bounded alternative exactly as stated in the note's seven rules: read-only GET /v0/previous serving the verified base only while a verified read is in flight, same profile, retained head equal to the flight's verified base, under one atomic publication owned at publish time; a distinct response shape; 404 the moment the flight ends, including on verification failure (the explicit unverifiable-tail choice); no change to /v0/status, /v0/wait, orientation, admission, the head clock or the kernel tracker; browser is the only consumer. Ratifying this proposal adopts A unless the ratification text names B; declining it leaves case C as today. It authorises no implementation by itself.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:33c335a14da70a7b2077bdb77b7527508188b550, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e855a8cacf6e182447f2cdd0589a676266854301 stale; retired bas